 "description": "EXPLORATORY, NOT A PRODUCT MODULE. A domestic free-to-play mobile studio selling in-app purchases through Iranian stores (Bazaar, Myket) and showing domestic ads. Behavioural relationships only, in index space (100 = before the shock). Revenue, wage bill, dollar-linked costs and cash are accounting identities computed outside the engine (research/iran_game_studio/study.py). Every coefficient was fixed before the historical benchmark was run, and every one is an expert_assumption: no Iran-specific estimate was found for any of them.",
 "notes": "Two exogenous drivers are held by events: the free-market dollar rate and how usable the internet is. The exchange rate reaches the studio four ways: dollar-linked costs (accounting, immediate), the general price level (partial pass-through, lagged), wages (follow prices, plus extra pressure from dollar-paid remote work), and players' real income (incomes catch up with prices only partly). Connectivity reaches players two ways: sessions directly, and a slow habit that recovers slowly after the network does - the mechanism by which an outage costs players after it ends. Payments are hit harder than play because a purchase needs the payment path to work end to end.",
